    ("abeyance", ["abeyance"], "搁置;中止", "/əˈbeɪ.əns/", "The new policy has been held in abeyance pending further review.", "新政策暂缓实施，等待进一步审查。", 4),
    ("abide", ["abide"], "遵守;忍受", "/əˈbaɪd/", "All citizens must abide by the laws of their country.", "所有公民都必须遵守本国的法律。", 5),
    ("ability", ["abil", "i", "ty"], "能力;才干", "/əˈbɪl.ə.ti/", "We value your ability to work under pressure.", "我们看重你在压力下工作的能力。", 6),
    ("abnormal", ["ab", "nor", "mal"], "异常的;反常的", "/æbˈnɔː.məl/", "Scientists recorded abnormal temperature rises in the Arctic region.", "科学家记录了北极地区异常的气温上升。", 7),
    ("aboard", ["aboard"], "在(船、飞机等)上;登上", "/əˈbɔːd/", "All passengers aboard the flight were asked to remain seated.", "航班上的所有乘客都被要求保持就座。", 8),
    ("abolish", ["abol", "ish"], "废除;取消", "/əˈbɒl.ɪʃ/", "Some countries have abolished the death penalty in recent decades.", "一些国家在近几十年废除了死刑。", 9),
    ("abolition", ["abo", "li", "tion"], "废除;废止", "/ˌæb.əˈlɪʃ.ən/", "The abolition of slavery was a landmark in human history.", "奴隶制的废除是人类历史上的里程碑。", 10),
    ("abortion", ["abor", "tion"], "堕胎;流产", "/əˈbɔː.ʃən/", "The new law on abortion sparked heated public debate.", "关于堕胎的新法律引发了激烈的公众辩论。", 11),
    ("abortive", ["abortive"], "失败的;夭折的", "/əˈbɔː.tɪv/", "The rebels made an abortive attempt to seize the government buildings.", "叛乱者企图占领政府大楼但失败了。", 12),
    ("abridge", ["abridge"], "删节;节略", "/əˈbrɪdʒ/", "The publisher decided to abridge the novel for younger readers.", "出版商决定为年轻读者删节这部小说。", 13),
    ("abrogate", ["ab", "ro", "gate"], "废除;取消(法令等)", "/ˈæb.rə.ɡeɪt/", "The parliament voted to abrogate the outdated trade agreement.", "议会投票废除了过时的贸易协定。", 14),
    ("abrupt", ["abrupt"], "突然的;唐突的", "/əˈbrʌpt/", "The meeting came to an abrupt end after the power failure.", "停电之后会议突然结束了。", 15),
    ("absence", ["ab", "sence"], "缺席;缺乏", "/ˈæb.səns/", "Her absence from the meeting delayed the final decision.", "她缺席会议导致最终决定被推迟。", 16),
