    ("independent", ["in", "de", "pen", "dent"], "独立的,自主的", "/ˌɪn.dɪˈpen.dənt/", "The country became independent over fifty years ago.", "这个国家五十多年前获得了独立。", 2092),
    ("index", ["in", "dex"], "索引,指数", "/ˈɪn.deks/", "The consumer price index rose by three percent last year.", "去年消费者价格指数上升了三个百分点。", 2093),
    ("indicate", ["in", "di", "cate"], "表明;指出;显示", "/ˈɪn.dɪ.keɪt/", "The survey results indicate a rise in customer satisfaction.", "调查结果表明客户满意度有所上升。", 2094),
    ("indicative", ["in", "dica", "tive"], "指示的,表明的", "/ɪnˈdɪk.ə.tɪv/", "Rising temperatures are indicative of broader climate change.", "气温上升表明更广泛的气候变化。", 2095),
    ("indifference", ["in", "dif", "fer", "ence"], "冷漠,漠不关心", "/ɪnˈdɪf.rəns/", "Public indifference to politics can weaken a democracy.", "公众对政治的冷漠会削弱民主。", 2096),
    ("indifferent", ["in", "dif", "fer", "ent"], "漠不关心的;平庸的", "/ɪnˈdɪf.rənt/", "The manager seemed indifferent to our concerns about workload.", "经理似乎对我们对工作量的担忧漠不关心。", 2097),
    ("indigestion", ["in", "di", "ges", "tion"], "消化不良", "/ˌɪn.dɪˈdʒes.tʃən/", "Spicy food often causes him severe indigestion at night.", "辛辣食物常使他夜间严重消化不良。", 2098),
    ("indignant", ["in", "dig", "nant"], "愤慨的,义愤的", "/ɪnˈdɪɡ.nənt/", "She was indignant at being accused of dishonesty.", "她对被指控不诚实感到愤慨。", 2099),
    ("indignation", ["in", "dig", "na", "tion"], "愤慨,义愤", "/ˌɪn.dɪɡˈneɪ.ʃən/", "The unfair decision caused widespread indignation among workers.", "不公平的决定在工人中引起广泛愤慨。", 2100),
