    ("inducement", ["in", "duce", "ment"], "诱导,诱因", "/ɪnˈdjuːs.mənt/", "The company offered bonuses as an inducement to work harder.", "公司提供奖金作为努力工作的诱因。", 2104),
    ("indulge", ["in", "dulge"], "沉溺,纵容", "/ɪnˈdʌldʒ/", "People often indulge in fast food despite knowing the risks.", "人们明知风险却仍沉溺于快餐。", 2105),
    ("industrial", ["in", "dus", "tri", "al"], "工业的,产业的", "/ɪnˈdʌs.tri.əl/", "The region has seen rapid industrial growth over the past decade.", "该地区在过去十年中工业迅速增长。", 2106),
    ("industrialization", ["in", "dus", "tri", "al", "iza", "tion"], "工业化", "/ɪnˌdʌs.tri.ə.laɪˈzeɪ.ʃən/", "Industrialization brought both wealth and pollution to the country.", "工业化给该国带来了财富,也带来了污染。", 2107),
    ("industrialized", ["in", "dus", "tri", "al", "ized"], "工业化的", "/ɪnˈdʌs.tri.ə.laɪzd/", "Many industrialized nations are now shifting to renewable energy.", "许多工业化国家正转向可再生能源。", 2108),
    ("industrious", ["in", "dus", "tri", "ous"], "勤勉的,勤奋的", "/ɪnˈdʌs.tri.əs/", "The industrious students spent long hours in the library.", "勤奋的学生们在图书馆度过了漫长的时光。", 2109),
    ("inertia", ["in", "er", "tia"], "惰性;惯性;迟钝", "/ɪˈnɜː.ʃə/", "Organizational inertia can slow down necessary reforms.", "组织惰性会拖慢必要的改革。", 2110),
    ("inevitable", ["in", "evitable"], "不可避免的", "/ɪnˈev.ɪ.tə.bəl/", "Climate change makes some coastal flooding almost inevitable.", "气候变化使得某些沿海洪水几乎不可避免。", 2111),
    ("inevitably", ["in", "evitably"], "不可避免地", "/ɪnˈev.ɪ.tə.bli/", "Population growth will inevitably increase pressure on resources.", "人口增长将不可避免地加大对资源的压力。", 2112),
    ("infant", ["in", "fant"], "婴儿,幼儿", "/ˈɪn.fənt/", "Proper nutrition is vital for an infant's early development.", "适当的营养对婴儿的早期发育至关重要。", 2113),
    ("infantry", ["in", "fantry"], "步兵", "/ˈɪn.fən.tri/", "The infantry advanced slowly across the open battlefield.", "步兵在开阔的战场上缓缓推进。", 2114),
    ("infect", ["in", "fect"], "感染;使受影响", "/ɪnˈfekt/", "The flu could infect half the office within a week.", "流感可能在一周内感染半个办公室的人。", 2115),
    ("infection", ["in", "fec", "tion"], "感染,传染", "/ɪnˈfek.ʃən/", "The hospital follows strict rules to prevent infection.", "医院遵循严格规定以防止感染。", 2116),
    ("infectious", ["in", "fec", "tious"], "传染性的", "/ɪnˈfek.ʃəs/", "Measles is a highly infectious disease among young children.", "麻疹在幼儿中是一种高传染性疾病。", 2117),
    ("infer", ["in", "fer"], "推断;推论", "/ɪnˈfɜː/", "From the report we can infer that demand is falling.", "从报告中我们可以推断需求正在下降。", 2118),
    ("inference", ["in", "fer", "ence"], "推断,结论", "/ˈɪn.fər.əns/", "The conclusion was based on a careful inference from the evidence.", "结论是基于证据的谨慎推断。", 2119),
    ("inferior", ["in", "fe", "ri", "or"], "次的,下级的", "/ɪnˈfɪə.ri.ər/", "Some consumers assume imported goods are inferior to local ones.", "一些消费者认为进口商品不如本地商品。", 2120),
    ("inferiority", ["in", "fe", "ri", "or", "i", "ty"], "自卑,劣等", "/ɪnˌfɪə.riˈɒr.ə.ti/", "He struggled with a sense of inferiority throughout his childhood.", "他整个童年都在与自卑感作斗争。", 2121),
    ("infinite", ["in", "fi", "nite"], "无限的,无穷的", "/ˈɪn.fɪ.nət/", "The universe seems to contain an infinite number of stars.", "宇宙似乎包含无限数量的恒星。", 2122),
    ("infinity", ["in", "fin", "i", "ty"], "无限,无穷", "/ɪnˈfɪn.ə.ti/", "The night sky stretched out toward infinity above them.", "夜空在他们头顶向无限延伸。", 2123),
    ("inflation", ["in", "fla", "tion"], "通货膨胀;膨胀", "/ɪnˈfleɪ.ʃən/", "Rising inflation has forced us to review our pricing.", "不断上升的通胀迫使我们重新审查定价。", 2124),
    ("inflict", ["in", "flict"], "施加,造成", "/ɪnˈflɪkt/", "Storms can inflict enormous damage on coastal communities.", "风暴会给沿海社区造成巨大破坏。", 2125),
    ("influence", ["in", "flu", "ence"], "影响;影响力;作用", "/ˈɪn.flu.əns/", "Consumer trends strongly influence our product design.", "消费趋势强烈影响我们的产品设计。", 2126),
    ("influential", ["in", "flu", "en", "tial"], "有影响力的;有势力的", "/ˌɪn.fluˈen.ʃəl/", "She is an influential figure in the publishing industry.", "她是出版界有影响力的人物。", 2127),
    ("influenza", ["in", "fluen", "za"], "流行性感冒", "/ˌɪn.fluˈen.zə/", "Outbreaks of influenza are common during the winter months.", "流感爆发在冬季月份很常见。", 2128),
