    ("insight", ["in", "sight"], "洞察力,见解", "/ˈɪn.saɪt/", "The study provides fresh insight into consumer behaviour.", "这项研究为消费者行为提供了新见解。", 2157),
    ("insignificant", ["in", "signif", "i", "cant"], "微不足道的", "/ˌɪn.sɪɡˈnɪf.ɪ.kənt/", "The error was so small as to be statistically insignificant.", "误差很小,在统计上不显著。", 2158),
    ("insist", ["in", "sist"], "坚持;坚决要求", "/ɪnˈsɪst/", "The client insists on receiving a written guarantee first.", "客户坚持先要拿到书面保证。", 2159),
